    /// <summary>16-bit A and W (f16): C = A W^T * sc[1]; Turing V5 (64 x 64 warp tiles, ldmatrix, register-staged double buffering). grid = ceil(M/256) * ceil(N/128), group = 256 (V7Threads). sm_75+.</summary>
    /// <summary>The same with the output columns split over three tensors: [0, N0) -> C [M, N0], [N0, N0 + N1) -> C1 [M, N1], the rest -> C2 [M, N - N0 - N1] (sibling projections of one input as one GEMM; N0, N1 multiples of 8).</summary>
